<title>GERMANY: German institutes detail pan-German economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>German institutes detail pan-German economic forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's six leading economic think-tanks on Tuesday gave the following detailed economic forecasts in their Spring report.</p>
<p>(All figures annual percentage changes unless stated):</p>
<p>					    1996	1997	1998</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN DATA:</p>
<p> Gross domestic product (real)    +1.4	+2.25     +2.75</p>
<p> Private consumption		  +1.3	+1.0	+2.0</p>
<p> Public consumption		   +2.4	+1.0	+1.5</p>
<p> Fixed asset investment	     -0.8	+1.5	+2.5</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>  Equipment			     +2.4	+4.5	+6.5</p>
<p>  Construction			  -2.7	-1.0	unch</p>
<p> Domestic demand			+0.8	+1.5	+2.25</p>
<p> Exports				  +4.9	+7.0	+6.5</p>
<p> Imports				  +2.6	+4.5	+5.0</p>
<p> Gross national product	     +0.7	+2.0	+2.5</p>
<p> Numbers in work ('000)	     34,465    34,110    34,220</p>
<p>  Unemployed ('000)		    3,965     4,280     4,160</p>
<p> Unemployment rate (pct)	    10.3	11.2	10.9</p>
<p> Consumer prices			+1.5	+1.5	+1.75</p>
<p> Unit wages costs		     -0.3	-1.0	-0.5</p>
<p> Total public deficits (bln)     134.0     116.0     108.5</p>
<p> Deficit as pct of nominal GDP     3.8	 3.2	 2.9</p>
</text>
